    title: "Watch: Moment a government building collapses into a river in Nepal amid floods",
    summary: "The municipality building in Baglung was left teetering on an unstable ledge due to floods before it fell into a river.",
    preview: "Massive flooding left a government building in western Nepal teetering on the edge of an unstable ledge before it fell into the Daram River. Witnesses captured the moment that the building in Baglung collapsed on Sunday, 27 September. Officials removed important documents and computers from the building before it fell, local ward chair Tej Thapa confirmed to the BBC. No one was injured.",
    body: "Massive flooding left a government building in western Nepal teetering on the edge of an unstable ledge before it fell into the Daram River.\n\nWitnesses captured the moment that the building in Baglung collapsed on Sunday, 27 September.\n\nOfficials removed important documents and computers from the building before it fell, local ward chair Tej Thapa confirmed to the BBC. No one was injured.\n\nLandslides and floods have killed at least 27 people over recent days, according to Nepal's national disaster agency, only weeks after a flash flood along the Nepal-Tibet border killed 1,400 people and left thousands more missing.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- NepalUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- FloodsUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Severe weatherUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
